    <<ad _ad>>
/* (Soccer uniform here in the future could be fun) */

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>!”</span> He says, falling off the couch and rolling to his feet, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Does this mean I can stay home and don’t have to sit at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span>’s stupid practice all day?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span>, who is sitting in the nearby kitchen tying his shoes, sticks his tongue out at his brother before waving to you. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I guess so.”</span> A deep voice laughs. You turn around and see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> walking down the hallway, typing away on his expensive looking phone, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nice to see you, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>. Thanks for helping out. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> said he would ‘die’ if he had to sit in on another of his brother’s practice.”</span> He laughs. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s because he’s lame.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> says running up, full dressed and ready for his soccer practice. <span style="color:Pink">He looks pretty cute in his uniform,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Soccer is the best. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s just dumb.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No, you’re dumb!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> says with a smirk, <span style="color:Pink">tackling his brother from the side as they begin to wrestle on the ground.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> sighs as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> rolls his eyes at you and chuckles. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Enough, you two, or else I’ll take you both to the studio instead and make you sit on your hands until I’m done.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> threatens. Both boys freeze, glancing to each other, before quickly getting back up. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> runs behind you, sticking his tongue out at his brother, while <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> does the same but behind <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>. You both laugh at the sight. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m sure <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> gave you the rundown. But I’ll need you to watch over <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> until I or <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> get home around 9PM. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> normally stays at his teammate’s house overnight, so it’ll just be you two. Make sure he is fed, entertained, and kept from destroying the house, and it should all be fine.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> says, picking up his rambunctious son by the back of his shirt and lifting him up into the air. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And he needs to be in bed by 8:30. Which means, young man,”</span> He says, holding his son’s face up to his own, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That you need to get that energy out, wash up, and be under the covers in your PJs BEFORE I get home. Got it?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But can’t I just stay up until you get home? Pleeeeassseeee?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> begs. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Maybe.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> sighs as his son gives him the pleading, puppydog eyes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Tell you what. If <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span> thinks you’ve been good AND you’re completely ready for bed, you can stay up until I get home. But if I hear you didn’t listen to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span> and tried to stay up without his permission well-”</span> <span style="color:Pink"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> spins his dangling son around and whacks his rear, causing his twin to laugh as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> blushes and tries to free himself.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll whack that butt of yours. Got it?”</span> 

