<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> nods, <span style="color:Pink">slipping out of his shirt and diving behind the couch to hide, peeking his eyes out and, feeling brave, sticks his tongue out at his father.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> responds by balling up <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s shirt and nailing him in the face with it. Not hard, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> falls back and reacts like he was just nailed with a baseball, except with less crying and more giggling. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We should get going though. Any questions?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> asks. You shake your head, thinking you got it. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Perfect! My number is on the fridge, so is <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s, so feel free to call if anything comes up. Have fun you two!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Bye <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> gives you a hug before following his father out, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Bye-Bye buttface!”</span> He sticks his tongue out at his brother as he runs out. You get the feeling those two were having a playful spat before you got here and chuckle. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Good luck.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> laughs, giving you a wave, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Try not to burn the house down.”</span> <br>
<br>
Once those three are gone and the sound of their car disappears into the distance, you turn around to find <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> struggling to get his shirt on. <span style="color:LightGreen">This is going to be an interesting evening.</span> <br>
